    # v402 (26/10/2026) -- THE DUAL-SCALE BRIDGE, THE FALL WITHOUT GEOMETRY AND THE CONDITIONAL EXPECTATION: three new kernel modules (PonteDaEscalaDual by Codex, ORDER 025, with errata E1 to E4 beside it; QuedaSemGeometria; EsperancaCondicional; provisional names), the computation of each with beta = alpha x sqrt(e) at runtime, the three inscriptions of 26/10 and the decisions of the management; the numbers are READ from the records ponte_da_escala_dual_v402, queda_sem_geometria_v402, esperanca_condicional_v402, cunhagens_v402 and kh_n1_cobertura_v402, never typed.
    # The box at the top (The Test of the Only Word, v397) stays where it is: the 4.44 rule is not touched. Nothing here moves the gate.
    _pd402 = core.get("ponte_da_escala_dual_v402") or {}
    _pv402 = _pd402.get("values") or {}
    _qd402 = core.get("queda_sem_geometria_v402") or {}
    _qv402 = _qd402.get("values") or {}
    _ed402 = core.get("esperanca_condicional_v402") or {}
    _ev402 = _ed402.get("values") or {}
    _cg402 = core.get("cunhagens_v402") or {}
    _el402 = core.get("external_ladder") or {}
    _cv402 = ((core.get("kernel_formalization") or {}).get("axiom_coverage_v392")) or {}
    _ok402 = all((core.get(k_) or {}).get("all_verified") is True for k_ in ("ponte_da_escala_dual_v402", "queda_sem_geometria_v402", "esperanca_condicional_v402", "cunhagens_v402", "kh_n1_cobertura_v402"))
    _i402 = lambda x_: str(x_) if isinstance(x_, int) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    _f402 = lambda x_, n_=6: (("%." + str(n_) + "f") % x_) if isinstance(x_, float) and not isinstance(x_, bool) else r"\text{n/a}"
    s.append(r"\section*{The dual-scale bridge, the fall without geometry and the conditional expectation}")
    s.append(r"\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{The dual-scale bridge, the fall without geometry and the conditional expectation}")
    s.append((r"\textbf{This round the v402 records did NOT all seal: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " if not _ok402 else r"")
             + r"\textbf{What enters.} Three new kernel modules: \texttt{TGLExt/PonteDaEscalaDual} (Codex's module, ORDER 025, copied byte for byte; it declares \texttt{maxHeartbeats 2000000}), \texttt{TGLExt/QuedaSemGeometria} and \texttt{TGLExt/EsperancaCondicional} (the names of the modules and of the five records are provisional: the operator names them), with " + _i402((_cg402.get("extras") or {}).get("n_bandeiras")) + r" flags, named declarations only; "
             r"three records with a function, read at the rite point right after the falsity of inertia (v401); and the " + _i402(len(_V402_VERBATINS2)) + r" inscriptions of 26/10, embedded by sha256 (\texttt{cunhagens\_v402}), all of them the operator's words. The kernel ladder reads " + _i402(_el402.get("n_theorems_clean")) + r" of " + _i402(_el402.get("n_theorems_expected"))
             + r"; the coverage of the \texttt{axiom\_report} reads " + _i402(_cv402.get("decl")) + r" constants and " + _i402(_cv402.get("thm")) + r" theorems, none outside the trio $\{\texttt{propext},\texttt{Classical.choice},\texttt{Quot.sound}\}$.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The dual-scale bridge.} \textsf{[DERIVED]} Takesaki's scaling law, $\tau\circ\theta_s=e^{-s}\tau$, is \textsf{[KNOWN]} and a field of the structure \texttt{DualScalingData}. The bridge realizes it as the longitudinal boost on $(E,p)$, with $c=1$ and $p^\pm=E\pm p$: $p^+\mapsto e^{-s}p^+$, $p^-\mapsto e^{s}p^-$, and $m^2=p^+p^-=E^2-p^2$ is invariant; the energy $E$ is the observer's \emph{reading} and changes with $s$. "
             r"The instance is the kernel's real structure (\texttt{momentumScaling}), not a local copy. $\star$ \texttt{lift\_mass\_not\_selected}: two invariants $\mu^2\neq\nu^2$ give two \emph{distinct} equivariant realizations with the \emph{same} $p^+$: the law fixes the null component and leaves the mass free. With \texttt{positive\_weight\_cannot\_be\_invariant\_mass} (a positive weight that scales by $e^{-s}$ is never invariant), "
             r"$H_\tau$ in its literal form (``$\tau$ is Newton's mass'') is \emph{refuted} in the kernel: $\tau$ can only be $p^+$, the light-front energy. \textsf{[REAL]} In this rite, with $\beta=\alpha\sqrt{e}=" + _f402(_pv402.get("beta"), 12) + r"$ at runtime (never a literal): $e^{-\beta}=" + _f402(_pv402.get("pplus_factor_at_beta"), 9) + r"$ and the rest state gains $\cosh\beta-1=" + _f402(_pv402.get("cosh_beta_minus_one"), 9)
             + r"$; the minimum energy shift of the null state is " + _f402(_pv402.get("min_null_energy_shift"), 4) + r" (the energy changes with the observer); with the same $p^+=2$, the squared masses $1$, $4$ and $9$ give three different realizations. These numbers are this rite's, they are not in the kernel.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Errata beside (by the management c1, in its own name; the kernel and the installed modules are not edited).} \textsf{[REAL]} \textbf{E1:} where the v401 text says ``the hypothesis $H_\tau$ ($\tau$ is Newton's mass and Einstein's metric), which no theorem uses'', read: the literal form is \emph{refuted} in the kernel; $H_\tau$ decomposes into named pending items \textsf{[OPEN]}: $H_{\mathrm{BW}}$ (the rapidity is the Bisognano--Wichmann modular time, $2\pi$), $H_{\mathrm{cal}}$ (this $p^+$ is the energy of \emph{one} body; the choice of $\mu^2$), $H3$ (Clausius in every null direction) and the debts of the 03--04/09 addendum (complete positivity gives the induced metric $(4,0)$, not $(1,3)$; $\operatorname{rank}c=4$, $H2$ does not come for free). "
             r"\textbf{E2:} ``\texttt{Inertial}'' in this instance is the \emph{zero vector} (fixed by every boost), not ``free motion''. \textbf{E3:} \texttt{rest\_energy\_eq\_mc2} is real algebra with explicit premises (shell, rest, $E\ge0$, $m\ge0$; $c>0$ is not used); the composition is \texttt{lift\_rest\_energy} ($c=1$), from \emph{rest}, conditioned on $\mu^2$ and on $\tau=m$ --- never to be read as $E=mc^2$ composed from the scale. "
             r"\textbf{E4:} the Codex delivery compiled against the Nós v400 kernel and the superseded copy of the inertia stone (only docstrings differ); the recompilation in the v401 kernel gave \texttt{rc 0}, 40 \texttt{\#print axioms} in the trio and an identical \texttt{.olean}. \textsf{[INPUT]} Condition C1 of the independent exam: only the \texttt{.lean} file entered, no other file of the delivery.")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The fall without geometry.} \textsf{[INPUT]} The operator, on 26/10/2026: ``o Um quando se põe realiza a operação'' (the One, when it is posted, performs the operation \texttt{input}, a word that comes in quotation marks in the saying), ``ao se inscrever, ele cai. a fase cai.'' (when it inscribes itself, it falls; the phase falls), ``então tem direção, mas não é gemétrica'' (so it has direction, but not geometric), ``a queda que eu quero traduzir não é força também'' (the fall I want to translate is not a force either; the spelling is his). "
             r"\textsf{[DERIVED]} Over the dual-scaling data, on a bare type (no metric, topology or geometric action): the weight falls \emph{strictly} and without end, $\tau(\theta_s m)=e^{-s}\tau(m)$, and the fall in nats is $s$; the arrow is the sign of $s$; the fall depends only on the weight, not on the carrier. "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} The floor is the \emph{post} (weight $1=\omega(I)$, the cut $a=0$), never the infimum $0$ \textsf{[management decision, ratifiable by the operator]}: $e^{-a}=1$ only at $a=0$ and the zero is never touched; delivery costs ($t\beta g>0$); the angular regime only reads (the S-matrix is $2\pi$-periodic and has no limit) while the face regime has a limit. Isotropy enters as a \emph{named} hypothesis (\texttt{IsotropicPost}) and it is load-bearing: without covariance nothing is transported (\texttt{covariance\_is\_load\_bearing}). "
             r"\textsf{[ONTO]} The $1+3$ reading: the direction of the posted One is the arrow of the fall of the phase, not of space, and the rest is isotropic; \textsf{[OPEN]} dimension $3$ is not proved. Question and answer of 26/10 (\textsf{[INPUT/ONTO]}, no verbatim file: \textsf{[DECLARED]}): ``does the posted One have a direction?'' --- ``the arrow of the fall of the phase, not of space''. \textsf{[REAL]} In this rite: the minimum cost $t\beta g$ is " + _f402(_qv402.get("min_cost_t_beta_g"), 6) + r", the maximum dephasing " + _f402(_qv402.get("max_dephasing_factor"), 6) + r" ($<1$) and the loss per unit $1-e^{-\beta}$ is " + _f402(_qv402.get("loss_per_unit"), 9) + r".")
    s.append(r"\textbf{The conditional expectation is the Name.} \textsf{[INPUT]} ``esperança condicional=nome'' (conditional expectation = name; 26/10/2026). \textsf{[DERIVED]} The typing already existed in large part in the kernel (\texttt{nameOp}, v162; \texttt{PostoAdendo.A1c}, v392); the stone is the \emph{composition}: in $M_2(\mathbb{C})$ the Name operator of $\rho^*$, $x\mapsto pxp+(1-p)x(1-p)$, \emph{is} the diagonal expectation; it preserves the One ($E(1)=1$); rereading adds nothing ($E\circ E=E$, the same form as \texttt{observing\_adds\_nothing}); its memory is a subalgebra; it is bimodular; and the mirror compression (Jones' relation, $e_D L_x e_D=L_{E(x)}e_D$) \emph{is} the Name. "
             r"\textsf{[REAL]} The index $1/\beta$ of the Name is \emph{conditional} on the kernel's two hypotheses (\texttt{hpp}, \texttt{hopt}) and no instance is built: with $\sin^2\theta_M=\beta$ at runtime, $1/\beta=" + _f402(_ev402.get("name_index_one_over_beta"), 4) + r"$; the diagonal expectation of the $M_2$ face has index " + _i402(_ev402.get("diagonal_expectation_index_M2")) + r", and the two numbers are \emph{not} identified. "
             r"\textsf{[ONTO]} The Name is \emph{three faces of one fixed object}, not three definitions: the operator \texttt{nameOp}, the Jones projector (the same thing seen in the GNS space) and the rank, which is the weight the expectation preserves; the kernel proves the \emph{links}, not an equality of types \textsf{[management decision, ratifiable by the operator]}. \textsf{[INPUT]} The four languages (probability, theology, linguistics, law) are the management's letter, with no derivation between domains; \textsf{[LEGAL]} the pointer CC art.~125 is to be checked with a lawyer. It is not proved that every conditional expectation is a Name operator; the stone is not a route to Lemma~3 and lives on the finite face (the $\mathrm{III}_1$ case is \textsf{[OPEN]}).")
    s.append(r"\textbf{Limits.} \textsf{[OPEN]} $H_{\mathrm{BW}}$, $H_{\mathrm{cal}}$, $H3$, the signature and $\operatorname{rank}c=4$; \texttt{IsotropicPost} in the curved atlas; dimension $3$; the contour instance with optimal $\sin^2\theta_M$; the identification of the dual scale with the flow of a physical body. The stones do not prove Newton's first law, nor the inertial $=$ gravitational equivalence \textsf{[KNOWN]}, nor that $E=mc^2$ is a kernel term. GR is the classical limit, not a rival, and $\beta$ does not renormalize local $G$. Validity in the kernel is not creditation; the gate does not move. The box ``The Test of the Only Word'' stays at the top, with its $5\sigma$ line.")
